---
import FailureDemo from './FailureDemo.astro';
import CodeExcerpt from './CodeExcerpt.astro';
import Notes from './Notes.astro';
import {
  sparcConstraints,
  sparcDatasheet,
  sparcDecisions,
  sparcDiagramAlt,
  sparcExplorerAlt,
  sparcInfra,
} from '../data/sparc';
---

<section id="sparc">
  <h2>SPARC</h2>
  <p class="sub">
    Sensor Platform for Academic Research and Community · in production since January 2026
  </p>

  <figure>
    <a class="frame" href="/sparc-architecture.svg">
      <img src="/sparc-architecture.svg" width="1120" height="590" alt={sparcDiagramAlt} />
    </a>
    <figcaption>
      Every box and arrow matches the code: three Rust binaries built from one workspace.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="cols">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        {sparcDatasheet.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{row.name}</th>
            <td>{row.description}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <figure>
      <img
        class="screenshot"
        src="/sparc-explorer.png"
        width="998"
        height="996"
        loading="lazy"
        alt={sparcExplorerAlt}
      />
      <figcaption>
        The SPARC web app: a week of hourly averages from one room sensor, served from the
        continuous aggregates.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <p>
    <strong>The problem:</strong> research and campus teams need reliable sensor data, but devices
    speak different protocols and no team should have to run its own pipeline.
  </p>

  <h3>Constraints</h3>
  <ul>
    {sparcConstraints.map((constraint) => (
      <li>{constraint}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h3>Decisions and trade-offs</h3>
  <dl>
    {sparcDecisions.map((decision) => (
      <>
        <dt>{decision.name}</dt>
        <dd>{decision.description}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <FailureDemo />

  <h3>Infrastructure</h3>
  <p>
    SPARC's backend runs as Podman containers behind Traefik on a Proxmox VM, with GitLab CI for
    builds and tests. Its Nuxt 4 front-end runs on our OKD cluster, deployed through GitOps.
  </p>
  <dl>
    {sparcInfra.map((item) => (
      <>
        <dt>{item.name}</dt>
        <dd>{item.description}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <CodeExcerpt />
  <Notes />
</section>

<style>
  .frame {
    display: block;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .screenshot {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  ul {
    max-width: 68ch;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
